      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "All 16 answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. q-83712: E[X]=8/3 and E[X²]=25/3, so Var[X]=11/9 and SD[X]=√11/3. q-84268: E[X]=4 and E[X²]=20, so SD[X]=√(20−16)=2. q-70105: det(A)=det(Aᵀ)=8 and det(I)=1; statements I and III are true, while II gives 17 rather than 16. q-158367: expansion along the fourth row gives determinant −12, so the volume is 12. q-90510: differentiating y₂=u cos(x) twice and substituting cancels the u cos(x) terms, leaving u″ cos(x)−2u′ sin(x)=0. q-102798: reduction of order gives u″−4u′=0; choosing u=e^(4x) gives the independent solution y₂=e^(2x). q-42732: the expected bill value is (4·5+8·10+6·20)/18=110/9 dollars. q-84066: the expected card value is (8·3+4·6)/12=4. q-112863 and q-6664: among the supplied choices, respectively −2 and −3/2 satisfy the rational-root theorem's numerator and denominator restrictions; being a candidate does not mean being an actual root. q-83826 and q-6671: respectively −7 and −6 violate those restrictions. q-112968: the distinct positive candidates are 1/8, 1/4, 3/8, 1/2, 3/4, 1, 3/2, 2, 3, and 6, giving 20 signed candidates. q-14144: using the given leading and constant coefficients gives positive candidates 1/3, 2/3, 1, 2, 3, 6, 9, and 18, hence 16 signed candidates. q-112990: f(x)=(2x−3)(3x+1)²; its distinct real roots sum to 3/2−1/3=7/6. q-75737: the displayed vector is u=(−2,−4), so Bu=−u/2=(1,2), shown by current image option 2. Each MA attribution below uses a contiguous verbatim span from that question's captured solution; no grade evidence is supplied.",
